  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding Essential Food Security and Health Services Project (Support for Afghan People)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be aligned with the following impacts: essential services sustained; economic opportunities and resilient livelihoods enhanced; and social cohesion, inclusion, gender equality, human rights, and rule of law promoted.8 The project will have the following outcome: access to food security and core health services for vulnerable Afghan people improved. There will be two outputs: Output 1: Food security enhanced ($200 million grant, comprising $100 million grant to FAO, and $100 million grant to WFP); Output 2: Core health services improved ($200 million grant to UNICEF).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide financing to United Nations agencies (Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations [FAO], United Nations Children&apos;s Fund [UNICEF], and the World Food Programme [WFP]) to help expand the delivery of essential services to the people of Afghanistan and secure the basis for the future development of the country through enhancing food security and maintaining provision of core public health services. Delivery of the project will be through the non-governmental organizations. As ADB placed on hold its sovereign and non-sovereign assistance to Afghanistan effective 15 August 2021, the implementation of this project will be outside of the public financial management system.</narrative>
  </description>
